{"id": "EUVD-2026-82035", "enisaUuid": "d0916adc-aced-344b-b1ad-bc84ea547505", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: validate RX band_idx before dereferencing phys[]\n\nband_idx comes from a 2-bit descriptor field (0-3) and was used directly\nto index dev->mt76.phys[] (size __MT_MAX_BAND == 3) and dereference the\nresult. A corrupt or reserved descriptor value could index out of bounds\nor hit a NULL phy on parts with fewer bands. Reject invalid band indices,\nmirroring mt7996_rx_get_wcid().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/493a029c205a994644327d554f0cfeb9651aba7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/535091c587268cc783608642838a655d828eefdd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f53ece876e1f3bbb3e18f48afc4af1ee967b16c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1c5cf8903bec5476a2233b4e45287b9a2213e02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2243778a5fae8329ab5f18e7adcd7e03b911a1b7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xvmg-v5vr-xr53", "CVE-2026-90374"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "090e0763-904a-3cdb-93de-5eeca1746c0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd21624c75a043e96812beadddf4f6f48e5 <535091c587268cc783608642838a655d828eefdd"}, {"id": "1161aaff-3468-3ffb-b8b1-817f33d44bf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1c6bff07-02cd-3996-90f2-7503712707b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}, {"id": "29949d9f-4e95-3120-b166-954ff3e3b4f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd21624c75a043e96812beadddf4f6f48e5 <2243778a5fae8329ab5f18e7adcd7e03b911a1b7"}, {"id": "3ed103ea-9cf8-397f-8945-71e030eab946", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd2162